<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in Minnesota."><title>Minnesota Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/google-analytics.php"; ?></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>Minnesota</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in Minnesota</h1><p>11 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Medical Assistance (Medicaid) &amp; MinnesotaCare</h3><p>Medical Assistance is Minnesota&#39;s Medicaid program, free or low-cost health coverage for children, pregnant people, parents, adults, older adults, and people who are blind or have a disability. MinnesotaCare covers many people whose income is a little too high for Medical Assistance, for a low monthly premium. Apply through MNsure at mnsure.org, or reach DHS Health Care Consumer Support at 1-800-657-3672.</p><div><a href="/programs/medical-assistance-medicaid-and-minnesotacare/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/medical-assistance-medicaid-and-minnesotacare/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Minnesota 211 (United Way)</h3><p>Dial 2-1-1 from any Minnesota phone, or call 1-800-543-7709, for free, confidential help finding local assistance with housing, utility bills, food, healthcare, and more. Minnesota 211, run by United Way, answers around the clock, every day, in many languages. You can also text your zip code to 898-211 or search at 211unitedway.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/minnesota-211-united-way/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/minnesota-211-united-way/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Minnesota Energy Assistance Program (EAP)</h3><p>The Energy Assistance Program helps income-qualified Minnesota households pay home heating and electric bills and covers emergencies like a broken furnace or a shutoff. Both homeowners and renters can apply. The program runs each year from October 1 through May 31 through the local service provider for your county. To find your provider, call the Commerce Energy Information Center at 1-800-657-3710.</p><div><a href="/programs/minnesota-energy-assistance-program-eap/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/minnesota-energy-assistance-program-eap/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Minnesota Family Investment Program (MFIP)</h3><p>MFIP is Minnesota&#39;s cash and food assistance for low-income families with children, and it is the state&#39;s version of TANF. It combines a monthly cash grant with food help and pairs most parents with MFIP Employment Services to move toward work. Apply online at mnbenefits.mn.gov or with a paper Combined Application Form (DHS-5223) at your county or Tribal human services office.</p><div><a href="/programs/minnesota-family-investment-program-mfip/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/minnesota-family-investment-program-mfip/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Minnesota Legal Aid (Mid-Minnesota Legal Aid / LawHelpMN)</h3><p>Minnesota&#39;s legal aid programs provide free civil legal help to low-income residents on housing, family, public benefits, consumer, and other noncriminal matters. Mid-Minnesota Legal Aid also helps people age 60 and older and people with disabilities. Call 1-877-696-6529 to reach intake, and find free legal information and your local office at lawhelpmn.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/minnesota-legal-aid-mid-minnesota-legal-aid-lawhelpmn/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/minnesota-legal-aid-mid-minnesota-legal-aid-lawhelpmn/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Weatherization Assistance Program (Minnesota)</h3><p>Free home energy-efficiency work for income-qualified Minnesota households: insulation, air sealing, and heating-system repairs that permanently lower your energy bills. Both homeowners and renters can qualify. The Department of Commerce runs the program through local service providers, and it shares one joint application with Energy Assistance. Call the Commerce Energy Information Center at 1-800-657-3710 to reach the provider serving your area.</p><div><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-minnesota/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-minnesota/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Debt &amp; Credit Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Minnesota Child Tax Credit</h3><p>Minnesota&#39;s Child Tax Credit is a refundable credit of $1,750 for each qualifying child under age 18, with no limit on the number of children. Because it is refundable, it can come back to you as cash even if you owe no tax. The credit begins to phase out once income passes $31,950, or $37,910 for a married couple filing jointly. Claim it on Schedule M1CWFC with your Minnesota return.</p><div><a href="/programs/minnesota-child-tax-credit/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/minnesota-child-tax-credit/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Minnesota Working Family Credit</h3><p>The Working Family Credit is Minnesota&#39;s version of the Earned Income Tax Credit, a refundable credit for workers with low income. It equals 4 percent of your earned income, up to a maximum of $379, and it can pay out even if you owe no tax. You claim it on Schedule M1CWFC with your Minnesota return, the same form that carries the state Child Tax Credit.</p><div><a href="/programs/minnesota-working-family-credit/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/minnesota-working-family-credit/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Minnesota SNAP (Food Support)</h3><p>SNAP, still called Food Support by many Minnesota counties, puts monthly food money on an EBT card you use like a debit card at most grocery stores and many farmers markets. Apply online at mnbenefits.mn.gov, the state&#39;s one application that also covers cash and other help, or file a paper Combined Application Form (DHS-5223) at your county or Tribal human services office. A SNAP outreach specialist through MNFoodHelper (mn.gov/dhs/mnfoodhelper) can help you apply for free.</p><div><a href="/programs/minnesota-snap-food-support/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/minnesota-snap-food-support/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Minnesota WIC</h3><p>WIC gives healthy food, breastfeeding support, nutrition education, and health referrals to pregnant and postpartum people, infants, and children up to age 5. Minnesota WIC runs through local agencies of the Minnesota Department of Health. Apply online at health.state.mn.us/wicapply, or call 1-800-942-4030 to find the WIC clinic nearest you.</p><div><a href="/programs/minnesota-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/minnesota-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Unemployment Insurance (Minnesota)</h3><p>Temporary weekly payments if you lost work through no fault of your own, from Minnesota&#39;s Unemployment Insurance program at DEED. Apply online at uimn.org, which is the fastest way, or by phone at 1-877-898-9090 for Greater Minnesota or 651-296-3644 in the Twin Cities, Monday through Friday, 8am to 4:30pm. Phone service is offered in English, Spanish, Hmong, and Somali.</p><div><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-minnesota/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-minnesota/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>